  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FT5">Definition <span data-tag="0FT5">24.26.4</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $(\mathcal{A}, \text{d})$ be a sheaf of differential graded algebras on $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$. Let $\text{Qis}$ be as in Lemma <a href="/tag/0FT4" data-tag="0FT4">24.26.3</a>. The <em>derived category of $(\mathcal{A}, \text{d})$</em> is the triangulated category </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  D(\mathcal{A}, \text{d}) = \text{Qis}^{-1}K(\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{A}, \text{d}))  \]
</div>
  <p> discussed in more detail above. </p>
